      n  samples  P(both ±MAX)  P(UNDECIDABLE)   median kappa    p90 kappa      kappa*
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     10     2000         0.000           0.000      1.000e+00    1.000e+00   9.007e+14
    100     2000         0.020           0.018      1.000e+00    1.000e+00   9.007e+13
   1000      800         0.672           0.196      3.000e+00   7.542e+305   9.007e+12
  10000      200         1.000           0.090      9.500e+00    4.500e+01   9.007e+11

=== interpretation ===
A column of positive uniforms has kappa = 1 EXACTLY. kappa explodes only when +MAX and -MAX
co-occur and cancel. P(+-MAX) ~ 1/600 each, so co-occurrence -- and undecidability -- grows with n.

analytic check: P(at least one +MAX in n=1000) = 1-(1-1/600)^1000 = 0.811; P(both) ~ 0.658  (vs measured 0.672)

Contrast with E2: every real TPC-H aggregate sat at kappa = 1.000-1.001 (decidable).
